===== J2-65-R10-HermitianReduction.py =====
HERMITIAN_CLASS_NUMBER_DET_MINUS2=1 (primitive classes)
ODD_PRIMITIVE_CLASS_COUNT=1
GENUS_COUNT=1
SPINOR_GENUS_COUNT=1
ISOTROPIC_CLASS_COUNT=1
H0_UNIVERSAL_REPRESENTATIVE=PROVED
FINITE_CLASSIFICATION=PASS
CANONICAL_PRIMITIVE_REP=[[0,1+i],[1-i,1]]
H0_REP=[[1,1],[1,-1]]
DIAGONAL_REP=diag(1,-2)
EXPLICIT_H0_TO_CAN_U= [[1, 1], [-I, 0]]
PROOF_STEP_1=For H=[[a,z],[zbar,c]], det=-2 gives a*h(x,y)=Norm(a*x+z*y)-2*Norm(y).
PROOF_STEP_2=If a!=0, e=(1+i-z,a) is integral isotropic; if a=0, e=(1,0). Divide by Gaussian gcd to primitive e.
PROOF_STEP_3=Extend primitive e to a Gaussian unimodular basis. Gram becomes [[0,beta],[betabar,c0]] with Norm(beta)=2.
PROOF_STEP_4=Normalize beta to 1+i by a unit. Replacing f by f+n*e shifts c0 by 2n.
PROOF_STEP_5=If c0 even then every entry is divisible by 1+i, contradicting primitive. Thus c0 odd and reduce to c0=1.
EVEN_DET_MINUS2_FORM=exists only imprimitive, e.g. [[0,1+i],[1-i,0]] has content (1+i)

