===== J2-65-R10-NormOneCongruence.py =====
GCD_G_u=1: uq=G+1
U_SIDE=N≡2 mod u^2; z_u=1+i gives Norm(z_u)=2 exactly; theta_u=z_u/(1+i)=1 has norm one
G_SIDE=N≡1-2AG mod G^2; z_G=1-AG (real) gives Norm(z_G)=(1-AG)^2≡1-2AG mod G^2
CRT=Because gcd(G^2,u^2)=1, Gaussian CRT combines z_u and z_G modulo G^2 u^2
COMPOSITE_NORM_CONGRUENCE_OBSTRUCTION=FALSE
COMPOSITE_SECTION=AUTOMATICALLY_SOLVABLE

